# GitHub Actions Conventions

## Node & npm

- Use Node 20 with `actions/setup-node@v4`
- Always use `npm ci` (not `npm install`) for reproducible installs
- Cache npm with `cache: "npm"` in setup-node

## Actions Versions

- `actions/checkout@v4`
- `actions/setup-node@v4`
- `actions/upload-artifact@v4`
- `softprops/action-gh-release@v2`

## CI Lint

- Use `npx @biomejs/biome lint .` — never `--write` in CI (must fail on errors, not auto-fix)

## npm Publishing

- Use `registry-url: https://registry.npmjs.org` in setup-node for publish jobs
- Set `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.COGNIGY_NPM_TOKEN }}` only on the `npm publish` step
- Always use `--access public` for `@cognigy` scoped packages

## Concurrency

- Use `concurrency` groups to prevent duplicate runs
- Release/publish workflows: `cancel-in-progress: false`
- CI workflows: `cancel-in-progress: true`
